# Copy to .env and adjust if your local ports differ.
# Base URL of the running Vite dev server (proxies /api -> backend :8080).
BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# DB-cleanup helpers (e2e/steps/**/*DbCleanup.ts, *DbSeed.ts) AND the seed-patch scripts
# (e2e/scripts/apply-patches.sh, e2e/scripts/teardown-patches.sh) shell out to `sqlplus` against ORACLE_DSN.
# On a host with no system-wide Oracle client, point SQLPLUS at the bundled wrapper, which forwards
# the call into the seeded-SCS-DB Docker container's own sqlplus (translating the host port
# 1525 -> the container-internal listener port 1521).
# Path is relative to nr-scs/frontend/ (where the npm scripts run); use ./scripts/... if you cd into e2e/.
# SQLPLUS=./e2e/scripts/docker-sqlplus.sh
# ORACLE_DSN=THE/default@localhost:1525/DBDOCK_01
# Container name of the pre-seeded image (default: real-data-seeded-scs-db). Set if you named it differently.
# SCS_DB_CONTAINER=real-data-seeded-scs-db

# Values that must match specific rows in the seeded database (see fixtures/common/seededValues.ts).
# The repo carries synthetic placeholders; export the real values (ask a maintainer, or look them up in
# the seeded DB) to run the scenarios that depend on them. Without them, those scenarios fail.
# E2E_INSPECTOR_GUID=                      # an inspector in scs_user_info_vw (un-dashed 32-hex)
# E2E_RISK_SEARCH_SCALER_CLIENT_NAME=      # client name on scaler risk assessment 723
# E2E_RISK_COMPLETE_SCALER_CLIENT_NAME=    # client name of scaler 019D
